A||||5||Adrift||Going to Junkyard - what upgrades/mods to look for?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||06-28-2001||06:16 PM||||I'm going to a few yards tomorrow and was wondering what parts for Mods / Upgrades I should be looking out for?<BR>My current ideas are:<BR>- Sway bar from front of fiero for back sway bar<BR>- Break calipers and what not from grand am for brake upgrade, as well as the cyl. from bronco (I think thats what you need for that break upgrade..)<BR>- Although unlikely, I would grab everything needed for a fastback conversion if I found one.<P>Anything else I should look out for? (Seats from other brands that provide better support? Higher effiency parts that clip on?<P>Thanks in Advance,<BR>Adrift<P>------------------<BR>My Dream Fiero, you ask?<BR>That would be a automatic '86 or newer V6 GT Fastback with T-Tops and A/C, fully running and for sale for under $1000 CAN. Know someone who's selling a car like this for this price in the Toronto area? PLEASE E-MAIL ME!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||06-28-2001||06:25 PM||||blazer master cylinder , not bronco<P>used brake parts?? scary.<P>although I did sell some calipers a while back that were used , they were just being used as cores.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||06-28-2001||06:28 PM||||I was thinking that too - new break parts aren't that expensive anyways. I fresh out of creativity for today - any other neat mods with junkyard pulls?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||06-28-2001||07:11 PM||||EGR valve cover, I forget which car it's off of. I've seen this mod, and it's a definite visual improvement, especially if your EGR is rusted!<P>anyone remember which car this came from? I think it was an Oldsmobile..???<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||06-28-2001||07:16 PM||||Also don't forget wings.. even if you don't need one, I'm sure you could always sell it to someone else. I think many Mustang wings fit Fieros, Firebird ones too.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
